{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"## Verified fixes\n\nAll three exact r3 reproductions are now fixed:\n\n- Nested semantic metadata through `yang/compile` throws an address collision instead of merging.\n- Reader-generated positions inside metadata disappear from both rows and reconstructed ASTs.\n- Metadata-bearing operand vectors throw `:slot-kind` for both affected tags.\n\nIndependently confirmed **23 tests / 170 assertions / 0 failures**.\n\n## Findings\n\n### 1. Blocking — new | [v2.cljc:633](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:633) | `not-empty` discards retained metadata on an empty metadata map\n\nReproduction:\n\n```clojure\n{:type :literal\n :value (with-meta [] (with-meta {} {:meaning 1}))}\n```\n\nBefore conversion:\n\n```clojure\n(meta (meta value)) ; => {:meaning 1}\n```\n\nAfter reconstruction:\n\n```clojure\n(meta (meta value)) ; => nil\n```\n\nThe recursive stripping preserves `{:meaning 1}`, but the enclosing `not-empty` then discards its empty carrier map. Thus the new recursion still loses semantic metadata before hashing or collision comparison.\n\nThis is admitted plain data. I reproduced it programmatically; ordinary reader syntax did **not** preserve this shape into the frontend. Its practical reach is narrower than the r3 cases, but it contradicts this function’s explicit preservation contract.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Collapse empty metadata to nil only when it also carries no retained metadata. Alternatively, explicitly reject this unsupported shape rather than silently losing information. Add a metadata-sensitive regression test.\n\n### 2. Non-blocking, deferred | [v2.cljc:657](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:657) | Custom-comparator sets do not reliably fail closed\n\nThe deferred case is subtler than “always throws.”\n\nConstruct two sorted sets using a comparator over `pr-str`:\n\n- A contains `(x)` and `[x]`, with both symbols carrying `{:meaning 1}`.\n- B contains `(x)` with `{:meaning 1}` and `[x]` with `{:meaning 2}`.\n\nThe comparator distinguishes list and vector print forms, although their elements compare equal under `=`.\n\nVerified results:\n\n```text\n(= A B)              true\n(same-meta? A B)      true\n(same-meta? B A)      false\nprojection of A,B    accepted\nprojection of B,A    address-collision exception\n```\n\nThe lookup repeatedly chooses B’s first equal element, missing the differing vector element. Consequently, traversal order determines whether corruption is detected.\n\n**Recommended fix/follow-up:** Keep this explicitly deferred, but describe it as potentially **silent and order-dependent**, not fail-closed. Supporting these sets requires one-to-one matching or rejecting comparator semantics inconsistent with `=`.\n\n## Other checks and outstanding scope\n\n- Forty metadata-nesting levels preserved semantic metadata and stripped positions correctly.\n- A record containing a metadata-bearing field still produces `dao.jing`’s record-rejection exception.\n- I found no cyclic metadata construction using ordinary finite persistent values. Custom host objects or self-referential lazy structures do not establish support for cyclic plain data.\n- The custom-set case is **not the only outstanding limitation**. `:root-reachable`, `:variable-scope`, remaining slot-kind validation, and inherited encoder limitations remain deferred. I reconfirmed that unreachable rows are accepted and disappear on re-projection. These remain separate validator work, not completed checks.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**No — not yet ready for Architect sign-off.**\n\nThe three r3 blockers are genuinely closed. The remaining change required by this review is to preserve or explicitly reject semantic metadata attached to an empty metadata map. The custom-comparator case and previously separated validator/encoder work can remain disclosed and deferred.\n\nNo files were edited. Verification was JVM-only."}}
